# Frontend

- Components that are reusable across features live in `frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx`.
- Prefer to split ui functions into smaller files. 
- Pages live in `frontend/src/features/[FeatureName]/[PageName].page.tsx` and set `document.title`. `main.tsx` picks the page from `location.hash`: no hash is the browser UI, `#/popup/<kind>` is a popup, `#/<page>` is a `ce://` page.
- Unique Components live in `frontend/src/features/[FeatureName]/[ComponentName].tsx`.
- Hooks and non UI functions live in `frontend/src/lib/[HookName].ts` or `frontend/src/lib/[FunctionName].ts`.
- Types live in `frontend/src/types/[TypeName].ts`.
- Every HTML element gets an `id` as its first attribute.
- Style with Tailwind. Merge classes with `cn()` from `frontend/src/lib/cn.ts`.
- The browser UI view sits behind the page views. Menus or panels that would overlap the page open through `openPopup` instead of rendering in place.
- Right Click Context Menus should have ContextMenu suffix in the name like `DownloadsContextMenu.tsx`.

```tsx
export function DownloadsPage() {
  useEffect(() => {
    document.title = "Downloads";
  }, []);

  return <main id="downloads-page">...</main>;
}
```

A new IPC call needs three pieces: a Rust command, a camelCase type in `types/browser.ts`, and a wrapper in `frontend/src/lib/browser-client.ts`.
